### Method 1: The "State Machine" Approach (Recommended)
This is the most robust method. Instead of just printing text, you store the current "scene" or "state" in a variable. When the player chooses an option, you update the state variable to the next scene.

**Pros:** Easy to debug, scalable, clear flow.
**Cons:** Requires a bit more setup code.

#### Implementation

**1. Define the Dialogue Data**
Create a class to hold the text and the options.

```java
public class DialogueNode {
    private String text;
    private String[] options;
    private String nextScene; // The ID of the next scene to load

    public DialogueNode(String text, String[] options, String nextScene) {
        this.text = text;
        this.options = options;
        this.nextScene = nextScene;
    }

    public String getText() { return text; }
    public String[] getOptions() { return options; }
    public String getNextScene() { return nextScene; }
}
